data.message:
A camera monitor has stopped publishing. This is NOT the same as a monitor reporting a fault - it means the monitor itself has gone silent while still showing its last value, so whatever it watches is currently unwatched and every other alert sourced from it is frozen at its last reading.
Stalled: {{ state_attr('binary_sensor.camera_monitor_stalled','stalled') }}
Ages (minutes since last publish): {{ state_attr('binary_sensor.camera_monitor_stalled','ages_min') }}
Each script publishes a bucketed updated_at every 600s, so a healthy monitor can never exceed ~10 min here. Check the HA core log for command_line errors and confirm the script still runs from a shell. {{ now().strftime('%b %-d %-I:%M %p') }}.
